  "query_preview": "with this update; however, it is very possible that \nthey may need to be upgraded to and Extreme Heat Warning within \nthe next day or two as heat index values will likely remain near\nor above 105 through the weekend. Today's convection may help \nto pull back on the temps, but that is largely dependent upon \nthe arrival time of the storms. Current thinking it will be late\nenough that all locations will still be hot!\n\nA frontal boundary is progged to sag southward into the area for \nMonday, which may briefly bring slightly cooler temperatures (upper \n80s to low 90s) for Tuesday into Wednesday of next week. At this \npoint, an break in the heat would be great!!",
